  "description": "Active non-default CUDA 13 vLLM pooling fallback for BAAI bge-small-en-v1.5, a public MIT-licensed English embedding model for semantic search, short RAG retrieval, clustering, and low-cost passage ranking. The active TEI CUDA 1.9.3 profile remains the lighter latest route with B200, H200, L40S, and RTX6000 support, but B300/SM103 is disabled there because the pinned TEI runtime exits before readiness with `cuda compute cap 103 is not supported`. This fallback keeps the same model artifact revision 5c38ec7c405ec4b44b94cc5a9bb96e735b38267a, uses the already mirrored official vLLM 0.21.0 CUDA 13 image digest sha256:a230095847e93bd4df9888b33dab956fa9504537b828a23657d2b26fed57b5c9, launches with `--runner pooling`, and selects CLS pooling with `use_activation=true` because vLLM 0.21.0 documents that this flag controls embedding normalization. The 2026-06-01T00Z TEI-vs-vLLM parity pass compared 10 general retrieval/control texts between TEI on L40S and this vLLM profile on B300 with min cosine 0.9999951641, max unit-vector delta 0.0006341759, max norm delta 0.0000000718, and 384 dimensions throughout. The same cycle's persisted B300 matrix probe passed with 3 warmups and 10 measured /v1/embeddings requests: 46.931 s startup, 72 ms client-wall p50, 73 ms p95, 361.11 tokens/s, and 0.98 GB VRAM. Hugging Face and vLLM caches are versioned under /mnt/data and Hugging Face token env is explicitly cleared because the artifact is public and ungated. Keep default_eligible=false and is_latest=false because this vLLM runtime is only the B300 fallback; do not enable non-B300 cells until each has its own matrix evidence.",
